From: Anton <17167061+ExtremeBoy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: limit the RX BA window to 64 on IPQ5018 and QCN6122

On a Xiaomi CR8808 (IPQ5018 + QCN6122, 256M memory profile, NSS Wi-Fi
offload) Wi-Fi 6 clients negotiate a 256-frame Block Ack window and REO
then drops part of what they send as "Frame OOR": ~20k per 30 s of
uplink in soc_dp_stats, about 17 % of the frames, and TCP stalled at
~40 Mbit/s. TCP ACKs of a download are hit too.

With 64 announced, Frame OOR stays at 0 and the download through the
NSS plane went from 84-200 to ~290 Mbit/s (80 MHz, 2x2 client). Limited
to these two chips: the others were not tested.

Signed-off-by: Anton <17167061+ExtremeBoy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c	2026-11-09 16:53:41.126528296 +0500
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c	2026-11-09 16:53:41.138528376 +0500
@@ -11328,7 +11328,15 @@
 	ar->hw->queues = ATH11K_HW_MAX_QUEUES;
 	ar->hw->wiphy->tx_queue_len = ATH11K_QUEUE_LEN;
 	ar->hw->offchannel_tx_hw_queue = ATH11K_HW_MAX_QUEUES - 1;
-	ar->hw->max_rx_aggregation_subframes = IEEE80211_MAX_AMPDU_BUF_HE;
+	/* IPQ5018 + QCN6122 with the NSS Wi-Fi offload: with a 256-frame
+	 * BA window, REO drops part of the uplink as "Frame OOR" (see
+	 * soc_dp_stats). Announcing 64 stops it.
+	 */
+	if (ar->ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10 ||
+	    ar->ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_QCN6122_HW10)
+		ar->hw->max_rx_aggregation_subframes = IEEE80211_MAX_AMPDU_BUF_HT;
+	else
+		ar->hw->max_rx_aggregation_subframes = IEEE80211_MAX_AMPDU_BUF_HE;
 
 	ar->hw->vif_data_size = sizeof(struct ath11k_vif);
 	ar->hw->sta_data_size = sizeof(struct ath11k_sta);
